# Check text out as LF on every platform. The Windows CI runner sets
# core.autocrlf=true at machine level, which turned checked-in files CRLF at
# checkout and broke the byte-equality contract tests that compare a
# checked-in generated file against the string its generator produces
# (published_v6_manifest_tracks_the_color_workflow_suite). Pinning LF keeps
# "the checked-in bytes" one set of bytes on both CI operating systems.
* text=auto eol=lf
